You changed files or ran commands this turn, but your last reply had no closeout record, so your stop is temporarily held. Do not start new work or push, merge, deploy or message anyone to fill in the record. Do only this: rewrite your last reply with the same conclusion, append a block like the one below, then stop.

<closeout status="done|not_done|blocked" merged="yes|no|n/a" deployed="yes|no|n/a">
did: <what changed, one sentence; up to three such lines>
artifact: <pr|commit|branch|doc|build|url|file> <reference>
delivery: <live|pr|merged|off|none; omit when no delivery standard applies>
unblock: <user|agent|other; omit without a delivery gate>
verified: <what you ran or measured and its reading, or "untested">
missing: <what you still need from someone, if anything>
waiting: <for status="blocked": who or what you wait for>
next: <optional on done: one short reply naming the proposed action in the owner's language>
</closeout>

Merged and Deployed: yes only if this exact change is merged or running in production, else no, or n/a; they are checked, and a false yes is worse than no. Delivery and Unblock only under a delivery standard; deployed but off by default is Deployed yes and Delivery off, with the blocker in Missing. Did: up to three plain sentences. Artifact: one per line; a file for the user is `file <absolute path>`. Verified: what you ran and its reading, or untested. Missing: only what someone else must supply. Blocked: name who or what in Waiting. Next, only when done: one short follow-up in the owner's voice before the final ---. Write the content in English.